task:ajcr-param-decouple --body "Title\n\nMessage"`; details: `horizon ps`
{
  "id": "I-1607",
  "status": "open",
  "body": "The roadmap's \"24 active items (max 8)\" warning is 14 CONE rows, not 14 competing fronts -- decide whether cones should be active at all, because nobody can act on the warning as phrased.\n\nMEASURED (janitor pass, run 0096). Of the 24 `active` rows, 14 have children and 10 are leaves. Every cone is unowned and is active because its subtree is in progress: AJC.jacobian (8 children), AJC.picrep (19), AJCR.w4-rep.datum (21), AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate (21), and ten more. The genuine parallel fronts are the 10 leaves, and 8 of those carry a live lane owner (pic-b, pic-c, pic-d, pic-e, pic-f x2, pic-h) with only `AJC.picrep.etale-rep.quotient-hom` and `AJCR.w4-rep.datum.chart-restrict` active-and-unowned.\n\nWHY THIS NEEDS A DECISION RATHER THAN A CLEANUP. Setting a cone to `pending` while its children are being worked is a lie about the board; leaving it `active` re-fires the warning every command for every lane. Neither is a janitor call. Two candidate resolutions: (a) treat `active` on a parent as meaning \"this subtree is the focus\" and raise/ignore the advisory cap, or (b) reserve `active` for leaves and let cone status be derived from the `n/m done` progress the renderer already shows. I did not change any status.\n\nThe 8 lane-owned leaves are consistent with the eight-lane round protection I-1482 describes, so the leaf count is not the problem.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "at": "2026-07-31T01:21:47.616570+00:00",
      "body": "Janitor re-measurement (pic-e 0095 r5): the analysis HOLDS and the count moved 24 -> 23. Now 15 cones (all unowned, all active because a child is in progress) and 8 leaves. I changed no status, per this item.\n\nTwo things worth adding rather than re-deriving. (a) Parent/child consistency is CLEAN: no cone has all children done with an open parent, and no done parent has open children — so the active count is the only roadmap warning, and it is the semantics question stated here. (b) Of the 8 active leaves, only 2 are held by a live run (pic-e, pic-c per `horizon ps` 0092/0095/0096); 4 carry owners whose runs have stopped (pic-b, pic-d, pic-f, pic-h) and 2 are unowned. Per I-1482 an owner is a live claim only while its lane is alive, but those lanes are between rounds of the same eight-lane round, so I did not clear them.\n\nThe task-queue cap has the same cap-vs-semantics shape; filed as I-1630."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-07-31T03:50:46.928187+00:00",
      "body": "Janitor pass (pic-e 0095 r6): I ACTED, within this item's own framing, and the count moved 22 -> 17. No semantics decision taken.\n\nYour dichotomy is cone-whose-subtree-is-in-progress vs genuine front. Five rows were in NEITHER: an active cone with no active descendant AND no owner anywhere in its subtree — `AJC.albanese`, `AJC.fbc.cosimplicial`, `AJC.fbc` (cascades), `AJC.pic0av` (6 children, all pending), `AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate`. Those are deferred, not in flight, so `pending` is not the lie this item warns about. Status-only writes; every summary is byte-identical (commit 3a511854e3).\n\nLEFT ACTIVE DELIBERATELY: all 8 remaining cones, each with a live-lane descendant; the 6 leaves; and `AJCR...abel-noninj`, which review-ajcr rank-elevated as the unowned hinge and which `pending` would misreport. The residual 17-vs-8 gap is your cap-vs-semantics question and still needs the decision you describe."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-07-31T15:43:48.213206+00:00",
      "body": "Fresh janitor measurement (pic-b 0099 r2): 13 active = 9 rows with children and 4 leaves. The cones are live Pic/Jacobian ancestry, the active DD-R/divrep chain, or pic-h's owned overlap-cocycle row; the leaves are owned by pic-b/e/f/g. No deferred cone or stale owner remains after clearing pic-b from done AJC.rr.extuniform. The residual cap warning is intentional."
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-02T12:26:59.836533+00:00",
      "body": "Fresh run-0108 measurement: 14 active rows = 8 parent cones, each with an active descendant, plus 6 leaves. The live owners are ajcr-param-decouple, ajcr-pic0-join, and ajc-kleiman-rewire; pic-e/pic-g retain queued fleet claims and one leaf is intentionally unowned. The target divrep chain is status-consistent; no row can be demoted without misreporting live work, so the residual cap warning remains semantic."
    }
  ]
}
